IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 26 and 26A.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively): the general power to alter the constitution (s 26) and the power to entrench provisions of it (s 26A).
-- s 26(4) is shown "[Deleted by Act 12 of 2002]" and is not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- Periods are counted by sg-periods.l4 only. A duty "within N days after X" is met by an act done on any day up to and including the last day (P2: `the date is not later than the end of a period after`); fork line F-I8.
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 26(1) to (1B): who may alter the constitution, and from when`

-- (1): "Unless otherwise provided in this Act, the constitution of a company may be altered or added to by special resolution."
-- A "may" whose gate is "Unless otherwise provided in this Act": where this Act otherwise provides the text points to that other provision (NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources, here to the other provision of the Act); a resolution of another kind is not addressed (NOTHING-kind: silent). Fork line F-I9.
-- src:4536 | 26.—(1) Unless otherwise provided in this Act, the constitution of a
-- src:4537 | company may be altered or added to by special resolution.
@ref s 26(1) (src:4536-4537)
GIVEN `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
      `this Act otherwise provides for the alteration or addition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1) the constitution may be altered or added to by the resolution` MEANS
    IF `this Act otherwise provides for the alteration or addition`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless otherwise provided in this Act" -- the other provision of the Act, not the subsection, says how the alteration is made (fork line F-I9)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of resolution`
         WHEN `a special resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "may be altered or added to by special resolution" does not say that no other resolution will do (fork line F-I9)

-- (1AA): "Any alteration or addition made to the constitution under subsection (1) is, subject to this Act, deemed to form part of the original constitution on and from the date of the special resolution or such later date as is specified in the resolution."
-- src:4541 | (1AA) Any alteration or addition made to the constitution under
-- src:4542 | subsection (1) is, subject to this Act, deemed to form part of the
-- src:4547 | original constitution on and from the date of the special resolution or
-- src:4548 | such later date as is specified in the resolution.
@ref s 26(1AA) (src:4541-4548)
GIVEN `the alteration or addition was made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the special resolution` IS A DATE
      `the resolution specifies a later date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later date specified in the resolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 26(1AA) the date on and from which the alteration or addition forms part of the original constitution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the alteration or addition was made under subsection (1)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of an alteration or addition "made to the constitution under subsection (1)"
    ELSE (IF `the resolution specifies a later date`
          THEN (IF `the later date specified in the resolution` GREATER THAN `the date of the special resolution`
                THEN JUST `the later date specified in the resolution`
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "such later date as is specified in the resolution" -- a date that is not later than the date of the resolution is not "a later date"; the text says nothing of it
          ELSE JUST `the date of the special resolution`)

-- (1AB): a special resolution adopting the model constitution "may do so by reference to the title ... or to the numbers of the particular regulations ... and need not set out the text".
-- src:4552 | (1AB) A special resolution adopting the whole or any part of the
-- src:4553 | model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to
-- src:4554 | which the company belongs may do so by reference to the title of the
-- src:4555 | model constitution, or to the numbers of the particular regulations of
-- src:4556 | the model constitution and need not set out the text of the whole or
-- src:4557 | part of the model constitution to be adopted.
@ref s 26(1AB) (src:4552-4557)
GIVEN `the special resolution adopts the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to which the company belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special resolution adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1AB) the special resolution needs to set out the text of the model constitution adopted` MEANS
    IF    `the special resolution adopts the whole or any part of the model constitution prescribed under section 36 for the description to which the company belongs`
      AND `the special resolution adopts it by reference to the title of the model constitution or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A special resolution adopting the whole or any part of the model constitution ... may do so by reference to the title of the model constitution, or to the numbers of the particular regulations of the model constitution and need not set out the text of the whole or part of the model constitution to be adopted."
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what a resolution adopting by reference need not do; it says nothing of one that adopts in another way

-- (1A): "Subsection (1) is subject to section 26A and to any provision included in the constitution of a company in accordance with that section."
-- src:4561 | (1A) Subsection (1) is subject to section 26A and to any provision
-- src:4562 | included in the constitution of a company in accordance with that
-- src:4563 | section.
@ref s 26(1A) (src:4561-4563)
GIVEN `the constitution includes, in accordance with section 26A, an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1A) the power in subsection (1) is subject to an entrenching provision` MEANS
    IF `the constitution includes, in accordance with section 26A, an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) is subject to section 26A and to any provision included in the constitution ... in accordance with that section" -- where the constitution has no such provision the subsection says nothing

-- (1B): "Despite subsection (1), a provision contained in the constitution of a company immediately before 1 April 2004 and which could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before that date, may be altered only if all the members of the company agree."
-- src:4567 | (1B) Despite subsection (1), a provision contained in the
-- src:4568 | constitution of a company immediately before 1 April 2004 and
-- src:4569 | which could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force
-- src:4570 | immediately before that date, may be altered only if all the members
-- src:4571 | of the company agree.
@ref s 26(1B) (src:4567-4571)
GIVEN `the provision was contained in the constitution of the company immediately before 1 April 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before 1 April 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(1B) the provision may be altered` MEANS
    IF    `the provision was contained in the constitution of the company immediately before 1 April 2004`
      AND `the provision could not be altered under the provisions of this Act in force immediately before 1 April 2004`
    THEN (IF `all the members of the company agree`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be altered only if all the members of the company agree" (a gate closed with "only if")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection reaches only a provision contained in the constitution immediately before 1 April 2004 that could not then be altered

§ `Section 26(2) and (2A): lodging, and the offence`

-- (2): "the company must, within 14 days after the passing of any such resolution or the making of any such order, lodge with the Registrar a copy of such resolution or other document or a copy of such order
-- together with (unless the Registrar dispenses therewith) a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered". One lodgement is taken to bring all the documents.
-- src:4575 | (2) In addition to observing and subject to any other provision of
-- src:4576 | this Act requiring the lodging with the Registrar of any resolution of a
-- src:4577 | company or order of the Court or other document affecting the
-- src:4578 | constitution of a company, the company must, within 14 days after the
-- src:4579 | passing of any such resolution or the making of any such order, lodge
-- src:4580 | with the Registrar a copy of such resolution or other document or a
-- src:4581 | copy of such order together with (unless the Registrar dispenses
-- src:4582 | therewith) a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered, as the case
-- src:4583 | may be.
@ref s 26(2) (src:4575-4583)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company lodged the copy` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered was lodged with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar dispenses with the copy of the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2) the company has complied with the duty to lodge a copy of the resolution, order or other document` MEANS
    IF `the company has lodged the copy with the Registrar`
    THEN (IF    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or the order was made` `the day the company lodged the copy` 14 Days
             AND (`a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered was lodged with it` OR `the Registrar dispenses with the copy of the constitution`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must, within 14 days after the passing of any such resolution or the making of any such order, lodge with the Registrar a copy ... together with (unless the Registrar dispenses therewith) a copy of the constitution" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it; and a copy of the constitution neither lodged nor dispensed with)
    ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or the order was made` 14 Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the 14 days have run and nothing is lodged
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days have not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then

DECLARE `s 26(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 26(2) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution, other document or order, with a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered (unless the Registrar dispenses with it)`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the day the resolution was passed or the order was made; the days run from the day after (P1).
-- src:4575 | (2) In addition to observing and subject to any other provision of
-- src:4576 | this Act requiring the lodging with the Registrar of any resolution of a
-- src:4577 | company or order of the Court or other document affecting the
-- src:4578 | constitution of a company, the company must, within 14 days after the
-- src:4579 | passing of any such resolution or the making of any such order, lodge
-- src:4580 | with the Registrar a copy of such resolution or other document or a
-- src:4581 | copy of such order together with (unless the Registrar dispenses
-- src:4582 | therewith) a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered, as the case
-- src:4583 | may be.
@ref s 26(2) (src:4575-4583)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 26(2) act`
`s 26(2) the company must lodge a copy within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 26(2) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution, other document or order, with a copy of the constitution as adopted or altered (unless the Registrar dispenses with it)`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the resolution, other document or order within 14 days after the passing of the resolution or the making of the order"

-- (2A): "If default is made in complying with subsection (2), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- Split site (i): an unmet element of the offence. JUST FALSE for the provision's own question (fork line F-I10).
-- src:4587 | (2A) If default is made in complying with subsection (2), the
-- src:4588 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:4589 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:4590 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 26(2A) (src:4587-4590)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(2A) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with subsection (2)`
      AND `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (2), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" (the provision's own question; split site (i), fork line F-I10)

-- src:4587 | (2A) If default is made in complying with subsection (2), the
-- src:4588 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:4589 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:4590 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 26(2A) (src:4587-4590)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 26(2A) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 26(2A) the person is guilty of the offence` `default is made in complying with subsection (2)` `the person is the company, or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000 "and also to a default penalty": no imprisonment (0 months), no "both" alternative, and the default penalty's amount is not encoded here
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for a person it makes guilty

§ `Section 26(3) to (7): what the Registrar must do, as it affects the company`

-- (3): the Registrar "must register every resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of a company". An official duty, encoded for what it means to the company.
-- src:4594 | (3) The Registrar must register every resolution, order or other
-- src:4595 | document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the
-- src:4600 | constitution of a company and, where an order is so registered, must
-- src:4601 | issue to the company a notice of the registration of that order.
@ref s 26(3) (src:4594-4601)
GIVEN `the document is a resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) the Registrar must register the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is a resolution, order or other document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the constitution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to register "every resolution, order or other document lodged ... that affects the constitution of a company"; the subsection says nothing of any other document

-- src:4594 | (3) The Registrar must register every resolution, order or other
-- src:4595 | document lodged with the Registrar under this Act that affects the
-- src:4600 | constitution of a company and, where an order is so registered, must
-- src:4601 | issue to the company a notice of the registration of that order.
@ref s 26(3) (src:4594-4601)
GIVEN `the document registered is an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of the order` MEANS
    IF `the document registered is an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an order is so registered, must issue to the company a notice of the registration of that order" -- for a resolution or other document the subsection says nothing

-- (5): "Notice of the registration must be published in such manner (if any) as the Court or the Registrar directs."
-- src:4607 | (5) Notice of the registration must be published in such manner (if
-- src:4608 | any) as the Court or the Registrar directs.
@ref s 26(5) (src:4607-4608)
GIVEN `the Court or the Registrar has directed a manner of publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(5) the notice of the registration must be published in the manner directed` MEANS
    IF `the Court or the Registrar has directed a manner of publication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in such manner (if any) as the Court or the Registrar directs" -- the manner is left to a direction that is not among the sources

-- (6): "The Registrar must, where appropriate, issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution."
-- src:4610 | (6) The Registrar must, where appropriate, issue a notice of
-- src:4611 | incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the
-- src:4612 | constitution.
@ref s 26(6) (src:4610-4612)
GIVEN `it is appropriate to issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(6) the Registrar must issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration` MEANS
    IF `it is appropriate to issue a notice of incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, where appropriate, issue a notice of incorporation" (a "where" condition: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); a duty, so JUST FALSE under limit 2 of the grant ruling)

-- (7): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation in accordance with the alteration made to the constitution."
-- The prescribed fee is a fact the caller supplies (the fee is prescribed outside the sources). "Upon" counts as "where" (the ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)); a duty, so JUST FALSE where a gate fails.
-- src:4616 | (7) Upon the application of a company and payment of the
-- src:4617 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a
-- src:4618 | certificate confirming the incorporation in accordance with the
-- src:4619 | alteration made to the constitution.
@ref s 26(7) (src:4616-4619)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar for a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26(7) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation in accordance with the alteration` MEANS
    IF    `the company has applied to the Registrar for a certificate`
      AND `the company has paid the prescribed fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of a company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue ..." (a gate with "Upon": the ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

§ `Section 26A: entrenching provisions`

-- (4): "'entrenching provision' means a provision of the constitution of a company to the effect that other specified provisions of the constitution (a) may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act; or
-- (b) may not be so altered except (i) by a resolution passed by a specified majority greater than 75% ...; or (ii) where other specified conditions are met."
-- src:4646 | (4) In this section, “entrenching provision” means a provision of the
-- src:4647 | constitution of a company to the effect that other specified provisions
-- src:4648 | of the constitution —
-- src:4650 | (a) may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act; or
-- src:4655 | (b) may not be so altered except —
-- src:4657 | (i) by a resolution passed by a specified majority greater
-- src:4658 | than 75% (the minimum majority required by this
-- src:4659 | Act for a special resolution); or
-- src:4661 | (ii) where other specified conditions are met.
@ref s 26A(4) (src:4646-4661)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of the constitution of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except by a resolution passed by a specified majority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified majority, in percent` IS A NUMBER
      `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except where other specified conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(4) the provision is an entrenching provision` MEANS
    IF    `the provision is a provision of the constitution of a company`
      AND (   `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be altered in the manner provided by this Act`
           OR (`the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except by a resolution passed by a specified majority` AND `the specified majority, in percent` GREATER THAN 75)
           OR `the provision says other specified provisions of the constitution may not be so altered except where other specified conditions are met`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'entrenching provision' means a provision of the constitution of a company to the effect that other specified provisions of the constitution (a) ...; or (b) ..." (a "means" definition; a majority of 75% or less is not "greater than 75%")

-- (1)(a): "An entrenching provision may be included in the constitution with which a company is formed".
-- src:4625 | 26A.—(1) An entrenching provision may —
-- src:4627 | (a) be included in the constitution with which a company is
-- src:4628 | formed; and
@ref s 26A(1)(a) (src:4625-4628)
GIVEN `the entrenching provision is included in the constitution with which the company is formed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(1)(a) the entrenching provision may be included in the constitution with which the company is formed` MEANS
    IF `the entrenching provision is included in the constitution with which the company is formed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of the constitution "with which a company is formed"; insertion at any other time is paragraph (b)'s

-- (1)(b) and (2): "at any time be inserted in the constitution of a company only if all the members of the company agree"; "may be removed or altered only if all the members of the company agree".
-- src:4630 | (b) at any time be inserted in the constitution of a company
-- src:4631 | only if all the members of the company agree.
@ref s 26A(1)(b) (src:4630-4631)
GIVEN `the entrenching provision is to be inserted in the constitution of the company after it is formed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(1)(b) the entrenching provision may be inserted in the constitution` MEANS
    IF `the entrenching provision is to be inserted in the constitution of the company after it is formed`
    THEN (IF `all the members of the company agree`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may ... at any time be inserted in the constitution of a company only if all the members of the company agree"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of insertion "at any time" in the constitution of a company already formed; insertion in the constitution with which a company is formed is paragraph (a)'s

-- src:4635 | (2) An entrenching provision may be removed or altered only if all
-- src:4636 | the members of the company agree.
@ref s 26A(2) (src:4635-4636)
GIVEN `all the members of the company agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(2) the entrenching provision may be removed or altered` MEANS
    IF `all the members of the company agree`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An entrenching provision may be removed or altered only if all the members of the company agree."

-- (3): "The provisions of this Act relating to the alteration of the constitution of a company are subject to any entrenching provision in the constitution of a company."
-- src:4640 | (3) The provisions of this Act relating to the alteration of the
-- src:4641 | constitution of a company are subject to any entrenching provision in
-- src:4642 | the constitution of a company.
@ref s 26A(3) (src:4640-4642)
GIVEN `the constitution contains an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26A(3) the provisions of this Act on the alteration of the constitution are subject to the entrenching provision` MEANS
    IF `the constitution contains an entrenching provision that covers the provision to be altered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "are subject to any entrenching provision in the constitution" -- where there is none, the subsection says nothing
